<title>USA: Pittsburgh Authority reviewing stadium options.</title>
<headline>Pittsburgh Authority reviewing stadium options.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pittsburgh Stadium Authority is considering whether to rebuild or renovate Three Rivers Stadium.</p>
<p>Renovation estimates run at around $121 million, while the price tag for a new structure is about $203 million. The city has already told the authority not to expect financial assistance.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, the National Football League Pittsburgh Steelers say something must be done. They would like to see a new facility built west of Three Rivers. The stadium authority is looking at alternative funding sources.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
